<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
  <meta name="facebook-domain-verification" content="wgmciky40v242pdx49k0pidinict9t" />
  {% render 'meta-tags' %}
  {% render 'organization-schema' %}
  {% render 'website-schema' %}

  <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="{{ 'gambetta-light.woff2' | asset_url }}" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="{{ 'switzer-regular.woff2' | asset_url }}" crossorigin>
  {%- comment -%}
    Switzer 500 is the weight every button on the site is set in, including the
    Add to Cart that is on screen for the whole visit on a phone. Unpreloaded it
    arrived after first paint and the primary control reflowed as it swapped.
    The other two faces stay unpreloaded deliberately: 600 appears only in
    headings below the fold, and Gambetta 400 is a display fallback.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="{{ 'switzer-medium.woff2' | asset_url }}" crossorigin>
  <style>
    @font-face{ font-family:'Gambetta'; font-weight:300; font-style:normal; font-display:swap;
      src:url('{{ "gambetta-light.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
    @font-face{ font-family:'Gambetta'; font-weight:400; font-style:normal; font-display:swap;
      src:url('{{ "gambetta-regular.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
    @font-face{ font-family:'Switzer'; font-weight:400; font-style:normal; font-display:swap;
      src:url('{{ "switzer-regular.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
    @font-face{ font-family:'Switzer'; font-weight:500; font-style:normal; font-display:swap;
      src:url('{{ "switzer-medium.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
    @font-face{ font-family:'Switzer'; font-weight:600; font-style:normal; font-display:swap;
      src:url('{{ "switzer-semibold.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
  </style>

  {%- comment -%}
    theme.css is the only global stylesheet: tokens, reset, base, layout
    primitives and the handful of components shared across templates (buttons,
    price, quantity stepper, photography plates, reduced-motion).

    Everything else is loaded by the section that uses it. This replaced five
    theme-sections-*.css files that were linked here unconditionally — they
    were one @layer block sliced across five files, so they had to load in
    order on every page, shipping hero, fold-sequence, safety-panel and
    fit-comparator CSS to /cart, /search and every content page.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'theme.css' | asset_url }}">
  <link rel="icon" href="{{ 'favicon.png' | asset_url }}" type="image/png">

  {{ content_for_header }}
</head>
<body class="template-{{ template.name }}">

  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

  {%- comment -%}
    The announcement bar and the header are one navigation system, so they are
    pinned as one element rather than two that happen to touch. The wrapper is
    what carries position:sticky, and it has to: a sticky element can only
    travel inside its own parent, and each section's parent is the
    <div class="shopify-section"> Shopify emits around it — which is exactly
    header-height. That is why the header was declared sticky and still scrolled
    away on every page in the theme.

    One element also means one z-index, one shadow and one scroll position, so
    the two can never separate, flicker apart or shift against each other.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="masthead" data-masthead>
    {% sections 'header-group' %}
  </div>

  <main id="main">
    {{ content_for_layout }}
  </main>

  {% sections 'footer-group' %}

  {% section 'sticky-buy-bar' %}
  {% section 'cart-drawer' %}

  <script>
    window.themeRoutes = {
      cartAdd: {{ routes.cart_add_url | json }},
      cartChange: {{ routes.cart_change_url | json }},
      cart: {{ routes.cart_url | append: '.js' | json }},
      root: {{ routes.root_url | json }}
    };
  </script>
  <script src="{{ 'theme.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
